{"batchcomplete":true,"query":{"pages":[{"pageid":63679224,"ns":0,"title":"Big-little-big lemma","extract":"In the mathematics of paper folding, the big-little-big lemma is a necessary condition for a crease pattern with specified mountain folds and valley folds to be able to be folded flat. It differs from Kawasaki's theorem, which characterizes the flat-foldable crease patterns in which a mountain-valley assignment has not yet been made.","description":"Theorem about origami","descriptionsource":"local"}]}}